[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102777] [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102778] [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102779] [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102780] {:db/id 17592186105747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" "question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/id #uuid "209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/math-academy-id "q-37776" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ 0x+y-6z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-6z=2\\,⇒\\,y=6z+2\n$$\n\nand substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-2(6z+2)+3z=-2\\,⇒\\,x=9z+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9z+2 \\\\ y=6z+2 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" "answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" "answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" "answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/id #uuid "b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9z+2 \\\\ -6z-2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/id #uuid "e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9z-2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/id #uuid "e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6z+2 \\\\ 9z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/id #uuid "ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/id #uuid "a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186106150 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=1 \\\\ 0x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=1 \\\\ y+3z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3z=2\\,⇒\\,y=2-3z\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-z=1\\,⇒\\,x=1+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1+z \\\\ y=2-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102776 :answer-field/correct "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" "answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" "answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/id #uuid "93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/id #uuid "e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ -2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/id #uuid "360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/id #uuid "c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/id #uuid "d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131487" :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" "answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" "answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" "answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/id #uuid "33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/id #uuid "25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/id #uuid "820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/id #uuid "56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/id #uuid "2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105748 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/id #uuid "6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/math-academy-id "q-73916" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-5z=-6 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-3y-5z=-6\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=-6+3y+5z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-6+3y+5z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/id #uuid "41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" "answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" "answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" "answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/id #uuid "21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3+6y-5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/id #uuid "2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/id #uuid "17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6+5y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/id #uuid "7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6-3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/id #uuid "b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105809 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/id #uuid "70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-131507" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+8y-7z=5 \\\\ 0x-5y+9z=-8 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=1,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" "answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" "answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" "answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/id #uuid "3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/id #uuid "66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/id #uuid "b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/id #uuid "4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/id #uuid "b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107082 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a system of linear equations where the corresponding coefficient matrix is singular. For example, consider the following system and its associated augmented matrix:\n![](images/1a/1ac826685473beeb7a7c0ee90465db019d0d5b70b1af562aa3469ae4f0a54007.svg)\n\nTo solve the system, we can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as usual. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/17/176e4c49ef19bb92d63190dc6674b66ee55b2fdb306293bae65b7f2b2935701d.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n![](images/a9/a9dd77f0f2ac0f7bd04b5e70fdca3b126d4eb34b0c929caca48c60f138bc644d.svg)\n\nThe **basic variables** are the variables of our system whose coefficients are the pivots of the row echelon form matrix. Let's illustrate the pivots of $M\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/1b/1b776faa6c69553ce04fbddc4e1aa45e18d7390a32ce34d9e0317b2fa83b8752.svg)\n\nThe pivots are\n\n- $m_{11}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $x,$ and\n\n- $m_{22}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $y.$\n\nTherefore, the basic variables are $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe remaining variables are called the **free variables**. We have only one free variable in our system, which is $z$.\n\nFinally, we can describe the **general solution** by finding equations for the basic variables in terms of the free variables. In our case, this means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTo do this, we apply the back substitution. From the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny - 3z = -5\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = -5+3z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-5+3z)+z=2\\,⟹\\, & x=-3+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n![](images/e2/e21bb2b83534152d6bf3d1c43efbd301b42717b975f1f9ebaa28ee4bc3ef31bd.svg)\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n![](images/de/de7a613bbbde25e555608ebc419106701d47875e238832eab7533bf87b0f1ce8.svg)\n\nGeometrically, this is the vector equation of a line, and any point on the line is a solution to our original system.\n\nIf we want to find some **particular solution** of the system, we simply choose some particular value of $z$ and find the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the line. For example, if we choose $z=0,$ then the corresponding values are $x=-3$ and $y=-5$ and the particular solution is $x=-3,$ $y=-5,$ $z=0.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/id #uuid "209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c"] ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/math-academy-id "q-37776"] ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ 0x+y-6z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-6z=2\\,⇒\\,y=6z+2\n$$\n\nand substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-2(6z+2)+3z=-2\\,⇒\\,x=9z+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9z+2 \\\\ y=6z+2 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"] ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb"] ["answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/id #uuid "b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe"] ["answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9z+2 \\\\ -6z-2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/id #uuid "e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6"] ["answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9z-2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/id #uuid "e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796"] ["answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6z+2 \\\\ 9z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/id #uuid "ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937"] ["answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/id #uuid "a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466"] ["answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/value "No solution"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/correct "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/choices "answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/choices "answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/choices "answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/choices "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937"] ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/choices "answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466"] ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb"] [17592186105747 :knowledge-point/questions "question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c"] [17592186106150 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186106150 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=1 \\\\ 0x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=1 \\\\ y+3z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3z=2\\,⇒\\,y=2-3z\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-z=1\\,⇒\\,x=1+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1+z \\\\ y=2-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186106150 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/id #uuid "93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c"] ["answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/id #uuid "e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff"] ["answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ -2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/id #uuid "360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529"] ["answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/id #uuid "c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0"] ["answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186102776 :answer-field/correct "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0"] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices "answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c"] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices "answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff"] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices "answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529"] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0"] ["question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/id #uuid "d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f"] ["question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131487"] ["question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] ["question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42"] ["answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/id #uuid "33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b"] ["answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/id #uuid "25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79"] ["answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/id #uuid "820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d"] ["answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/id #uuid "56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2"] ["answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/id #uuid "2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395"] ["answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/correct "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/choices "answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/choices "answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/choices "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/choices "answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2"] ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395"] ["question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42"] [17592186105747 :knowledge-point/questions "question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f"] ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/id #uuid "6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae"] ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/math-academy-id "q-73916"] ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-5z=-6 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-3y-5z=-6\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=-6+3y+5z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-6+3y+5z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/id #uuid "41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb"] ["answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/id #uuid "21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342"] ["answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3+6y-5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/id #uuid "2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d"] ["answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/id #uuid "17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95"] ["answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6+5y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/id #uuid "7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276"] ["answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6-3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/id #uuid "b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09"] ["answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/value "No solution"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/correct "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/choices "answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/choices "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/choices "answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/choices "answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276"] ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/choices "answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09"] ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb"] [17592186105748 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae"] ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/id #uuid "70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee"] ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-131507"] ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+8y-7z=5 \\\\ 0x-5y+9z=-8 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=1,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1"] ["answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/id #uuid "3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb"] ["answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/id #uuid "66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27"] ["answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/id #uuid "b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41"] ["answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/id #uuid "4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f"] ["answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/id #uuid "b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c"] ["answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/value "No solution"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/correct "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/choices "answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/choices "answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/choices "answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/choices "answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f"] ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/choices "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c"] ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1"] [17592186105809 :knowledge-point/questions "question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee"] [17592186107082 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a system of linear equations where the corresponding coefficient matrix is singular. For example, consider the following system and its associated augmented matrix:\n![](images/1a/1ac826685473beeb7a7c0ee90465db019d0d5b70b1af562aa3469ae4f0a54007.svg)\n\nTo solve the system, we can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as usual. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/17/176e4c49ef19bb92d63190dc6674b66ee55b2fdb306293bae65b7f2b2935701d.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n![](images/a9/a9dd77f0f2ac0f7bd04b5e70fdca3b126d4eb34b0c929caca48c60f138bc644d.svg)\n\nThe **basic variables** are the variables of our system whose coefficients are the pivots of the row echelon form matrix. Let's illustrate the pivots of $M\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/1b/1b776faa6c69553ce04fbddc4e1aa45e18d7390a32ce34d9e0317b2fa83b8752.svg)\n\nThe pivots are\n\n- $m_{11}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $x,$ and\n\n- $m_{22}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $y.$\n\nTherefore, the basic variables are $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe remaining variables are called the **free variables**. We have only one free variable in our system, which is $z$.\n\nFinally, we can describe the **general solution** by finding equations for the basic variables in terms of the free variables. In our case, this means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTo do this, we apply the back substitution. From the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny - 3z = -5\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = -5+3z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-5+3z)+z=2\\,⟹\\, & x=-3+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n![](images/e2/e21bb2b83534152d6bf3d1c43efbd301b42717b975f1f9ebaa28ee4bc3ef31bd.svg)\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n![](images/de/de7a613bbbde25e555608ebc419106701d47875e238832eab7533bf87b0f1ce8.svg)\n\nGeometrically, this is the vector equation of a line, and any point on the line is a solution to our original system.\n\nIf we want to find some **particular solution** of the system, we simply choose some particular value of $z$ and find the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the line. For example, if we choose $z=0,$ then the corresponding values are $x=-3$ and $y=-5$ and the particular solution is $x=-3,$ $y=-5,$ $z=0.$"]] "retractions" [[17592186106150 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$M = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102777] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102778] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102779] [17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102780] [17592186107082 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a system of linear equations where the corresponding coefficient matrix is singular. For example, consider the following system and its associated augmented matrix:\n![](images/1a/1ac826685473beeb7a7c0ee90465db019d0d5b70b1af562aa3469ae4f0a54007.svg)\n\nTo solve the system, we can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as usual. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/17/176e4c49ef19bb92d63190dc6674b66ee55b2fdb306293bae65b7f2b2935701d.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n![](images/a9/a9dd77f0f2ac0f7bd04b5e70fdca3b126d4eb34b0c929caca48c60f138bc644d.svg)\n\nThe **basic variables** are the variables of our system whose coefficients are the pivots of the row echelon form matrix. Let's illustrate the pivots of $M\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/1b/1b776faa6c69553ce04fbddc4e1aa45e18d7390a32ce34d9e0317b2fa83b8752.svg)\n\nThe pivots are\n\n- $m_{11}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $x,$ and\n\n- $m_{22}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $y.$\n\nTherefore, the basic variables are $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe remaining variables are called the **free variables**. We have only one free variable in our system, which is $z$.\n\nFinally, we can describe the **general solution** by finding equations for the basic variables in terms of the free variables. In our case, this means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTo do this, we apply the back substitution. From the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny - 3z = -5\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = -5+3z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-5+3z)+z=2\\,⟹\\, & x=-3+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n![](images/e2/e21bb2b83534152d6bf3d1c43efbd301b42717b975f1f9ebaa28ee4bc3ef31bd.svg)\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n![](images/de/de7a613bbbde25e555608ebc419106701d47875e238832eab7533bf87b0f1ce8.svg)\n\nGeometrically, this is the vector equation of a line, and any point on the line is a solution to our original system.\n\nIf we want to find some **particular solution** of the system, we simply choose some particular value of $z$ and find the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the line. For example, if we choose $z=0,$ then the corresponding values are $x=-3$ and $y=-5$ and the particular solution is $x=-3,$ $y=-5,$ $z=0.$"]]}]